 "result": "maze.py is a BFS over a bytearray grid padded with a '#' border. Visited cells are marked by overwriting them with '#' (35), which removes a separate visited-array lookup per neighbour. It reads stdin as bytes, prints the shortest S-to-E distance, or -1 when there is no path or S/E is missing. It matches all three sample outputs (2008, -1, 78). It passed assay at baseline 2.936, and the folded-visited variant was adopted with a +9% gain over the prior body. I'm stopping here because the job is done and further gains would be small.",
